Celvex Spectra 480 warmed up for 30 min; lamp hours 1564.
Substrate stock 100 mM in assay buffer; serial dilutions made fresh at 10:40.
Pathlength correction is on in the reader template (does not matter for slopes we report).
Kinetic window 0-3 min used for slopes; R² of the linear fits all above 0.997 except where noted.
Took 5 photos of the plate for the ELN; filenames IMG_3236 onwards.
Shared the reader with the teaching group from 15:00; nothing else of note.

Addendum (2031-05-06, 16:21): My 2031-05-05 rates are per minute, not per second; the µM s⁻¹ in the rate column header is a leftover from the old template. Read them as uM/min.

Addendum (2031-05-07, 14:40): Late note for 2031-05-05, the ninth study well (counting from the left) of plate 8, row B: not a spill: the enzyme went into that well twice.

Addendum (2031-05-07, 17:26): Plate 13 row B: the highest-[S] well came out over range (OVR) in the reader log; my 2031-05-05 sheet does not show the flag.
